
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.TeleportAgentHome(AvatarID: uuid)`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`llTeleportAgentHome(key AvatarID);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Teleports <b>avatar</b> on owner&#39;s land to their home location without any warning, similar to a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/w/index.php?title=God_Summons&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1" target="_blank">God Summons</a> or <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Death" target="_blank">dying</a>.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>uuid</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>key</span></td>
          <td>AvatarID / <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Parameters/avatar" target="_blank">avatar</a></td>
          <td>avatar <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/UUID" target="_blank">UUID</a> that is in the same <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Region" target="_blank">region</a></td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>avatar</li>
        <li>land_moderation</li>
        <li>teleport</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Sleep</span><span class="tech-val">5s</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">100</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">158</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <p>Generally, the object owner must also be the land owner but there is an exception for land deeded to a group for group members with the &quot;Eject and freeze Residents on parcels&quot; ability. See <a href="#Ownership_Limitations" target="_blank">#Ownership Limitations</a> for details.</p>
  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <h3>Ownership Limitations</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>If the land under the object is owned by an individual, the script must be owned by the same individual.</li>
    <li>If the land under the object is deeded to a group the object will need to satisfy one of the following:
    <ul>
      <li>The object is deeded to the same group.</li>
      <li>The object owner must have &quot;Eject and freeze Residents on parcels&quot; ability in the group and be connected to the sim[[1]](#footnote_1).</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This function causes the script to sleep for 5.0 seconds.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

local function main()
    -- floattext is red and opaque
    ll.SetText("Don't touch me!", vector(1.0, 0.0, 0.0), 1.0)
end

function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local num_detected = #events
    local id = ll.DetectedKey(0)

    ll.TeleportAgentHome(id)
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        // floattext is red and opaque
        llSetText("Don't touch me!", <1.0, 0.0, 0.0>, 1.0);
    }

    touch_start(integer num_detected)
    {
        key id = llDetectedKey(0);

        llTeleportAgentHome(id);
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
